Bundled in the installers
- CPython 3.13 runtime, from python-build-standalone (astral-sh) — Python Software Foundation License
- Tauri 2 desktop shell — MIT or Apache-2.0
- Microsoft WebView2 runtime (Windows; bootstrapper downloaded at install time when missing) — Microsoft terms
- Crocodile market-data engine 0.3.2, vendored as server/vendor/crocodile-0.3.2-py3-none-any.whl — Apache-2.0 as its wheel metadata declares; the licence file ships inside the wheel (dist-info/licenses/LICENSE)
- Python dependencies: aiohttp (Apache-2.0), certifi (MPL-2.0), fastapi (MIT), msgspec (BSD-3-Clause), numpy (BSD-3-Clause), polars (MIT), uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause), ccxt (MIT)
- Packages that the market-data engine and ccxt install with them: pandas (BSD-3-Clause), pyarrow (Apache-2.0; not shipped in the Windows arm64 installer), yfinance (Apache-2.0), beautifulsoup4 (MIT), duckdb (MIT, used by the intelligence store), curl_cffi (MIT), cryptography (Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause)
- Client libraries: React and React DOM (MIT), zustand (MIT)
- Typefaces bundled with the client: Inter, JetBrains Mono and Pixelify Sans, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  Their licence texts are in the source repository at client/src/assets/fonts/LICENSE-inter.txt,
  client/src/assets/fonts/LICENSE-jetbrains-mono.txt and client/src/assets/fonts/LICENSE-pixelify-sans.txt, and each release's THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt includes them.

Build and test tooling (not shipped)
- Vite, Vitest, Playwright, TypeScript, ESLint and typescript-eslint, pytest, ruff

Market-data providers (used at run time, not bundled)
- Binance, Bybit, Coinbase, Deribit and OKX public endpoints; Yahoo Finance and Google Finance endpoints.
  Feed modules for FRED (St. Louis Fed), FINRA, House Stock Watcher, OpenSky Network, USAspending and
  Greenhouse job boards exist, but no producer runs for them in this build, so they are not contacted.
  Each provider's terms apply. See the README section on data providers and attribution.
